cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CellForge: Agentic Design of Virtual Cell Models"
message: "If you use CellForge, please cite both the software and the preprint below."
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/gersteinlab/CellForge"
url: "https://github.com/gersteinlab/CellForge"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-07-19
abstract: >-
  CellForge is a multi-agent framework that autonomously designs computational
  methods for single-cell omics. Given a dataset and a research question, it
  performs literature-grounded task analysis, coordinates domain-expert agents
  through a peer-review debate to converge on a model architecture, and
  generates verified, executable training code.
keywords:
  - single-cell omics
  - virtual cell models
  - perturbation prediction
  - multi-agent systems
  - large language models
  - automated machine learning
  - computational biology
